      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T07:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is more related with the other bit hardware can set, e.g., dirty bit. It is possible to clobber the dirty bit if the operation is not atomic? E.g., the hardware just set dirty bit right before loading the PTE by the `pte_mkold`, and then the `pte_mkold` clears access bit based on the old PTE and write it back, make the dirty bit lost.",
      "parentUuid": "1843d1ca_ab8af2cb",
      "revId": "4d39346dee7059bcc8dc59684e16a6a7906390b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
